# C64 C Projects — Claude Guide

## Project overview

This project writes C programs for the Commodore 64 using the VS64 VS Code
extension and the cc65 cross-compiler suite. Programs are compiled by VS64's
build system and tested on real hardware via a C64 Ultimate cartridge or in
the VICE emulator, both accessible through the C64 Bridge MCP server.
The C64 Ultimate is a full FPGA recreation of the Commodore 64 — not a cartridge
in an original C64.

---

## Toolchain

| Tool | Details |
|------|---------|
| **Compiler suite** | cc65 — C cross-compiler suite targeting 6502/C64 (cc65 + ca65 + ld65) |
| **Convenience driver** | `cl65` — combines compile + assemble + link in one command |
| **VS Code extension** | VS64 (rosc.vs64) — project system, build integration, debugger |
| **Emulator** | VICE (standard build, runs with a visible window) |
| **Real hardware** | C64 Ultimate computer (FPGA-based C64 replica) |
| **MCP bridge** | C64 Bridge MCP server — targets VICE or the C64 Ultimate computer |
| **cc65 install** | `C:\bin\cc65-snapshot-win32\` (snapshot build; `cl65.exe` is in `bin\`) |
| **cc65 binaries** | Must be on `PATH` (or set `vs64.cc65InstallDir` in VS Code Settings) |
| **cc65 includes** | `<install>\include\` and `<install>\include\c64\` |

> **Verify your install** — if VS64 can't find cc65, open VS Code Settings and
> search for `vs64.cc65InstallDir`. Point it at your actual install folder.
> Alternatively, ensure `cl65.exe` is on your system `PATH`.

