## VS64 project file (vs64.json)

cc65 projects are driven by a `vs64.json` in the project root. Minimal example:

```json
{
    "toolkit": "cc65",
    "machine": "c64",
    "sources": ["src/main.c"],
    "output": "build/main.prg"
}
```

Additional compiler arguments go in the `"args"` array:

```json
{
    "toolkit": "cc65",
    "machine": "c64",
    "sources": ["src/main.c"],
    "output": "build/main.prg",
    "args": ["-O", "-Oi", "-Or"]
}
```

Common `args` flags:

| Flag | Effect |
|------|--------|
| *(no flags)* | No optimization — best for debugging |
| `-O` | Basic optimization |
| `-Oi` | Inline some subroutine calls |
| `-Or` | Enable register variables (use zero page for locals) |
| `-Os` | Inline standard library functions |
| `-O -Oi -Or -Os` | All optimizations — use for final builds |
| `--debug-info` | Emit source-level debug info into the binary |
| `--dbgfile build/main.dbg` | Write VICE-compatible debug symbol file (**not supported by snapshot build**) |
| `--mapfile build/main.map` | Write linker map (addresses of all symbols) |

> **Snapshot build note:** The cc65 snapshot at `C:\bin\cc65-snapshot-win32\` does **not** support
> `--dbgfile` on `cl65`. Omit it; use `--mapfile` for crash diagnosis instead.

