## Build and run

VS64 handles the build automatically when you save or via **Run → Run and Debug**.
For manual builds using the `cl65` convenience driver (use the full path since it's not on PATH):

```
& "C:\bin\cc65-snapshot-win32\bin\cl65.exe" -t c64 -O --mapfile build/main.map -o "build/main.prg" src/main.c
```

Or separate steps (useful when mixing C and assembly sources):

```
cc65 -t c64 -O -o build/main.s  src/main.c
ca65 -t c64      -o build/main.o  build/main.s
ld65 -t c64      -o build/main.prg build/main.o c64.lib
```

cc65 produces:
- `build/main.prg` — the loadable C64 program
- `build/main.map` — linker map with symbol addresses (add `--mapfile`)
- `build/main.dbg` — VICE-loadable debug symbols (add `--dbgfile`)
- `build/main.s` — intermediate assembly (retained with `-S` on cc65 directly)

**When VICE reports a crash, open the `.map` file** — it lists the address of
every C function and global variable so you can cross-reference the PC register.
Load the `.dbg` file into VICE's monitor (`ll "main.dbg"`) for symbol names.

