## C64 reference resources

| Resource | What it covers |
|----------|---------------|
| **Commodore 64 Programmer's Reference Guide** (CBM, 1982) | Official memory map, VIC-II/SID/CIA registers, PETSCII tables |
| **Mapping the Commodore 64** (Sheldon Leemon, 1984) | Annotated map of every address $0000–$FFFF |
| **cc65 Users Guide** | https://cc65.github.io/doc/cc65.html |
| **cc65 C64 library docs** | https://cc65.github.io/doc/c64.html |
| **cc65 GitHub** | https://github.com/cc65/cc65 |
| **c64-wiki.com** | Online, searchable — PETSCII, KERNAL, hardware registers |
| **C64 Bridge MCP reference** | https://github.com/chrisgleissner/c64bridge |

When writing code that touches hardware registers (VIC-II, SID, CIA, color RAM),
check Mapping the C64 for the exact address and the Programmer's Reference Guide
for the bit layout. Then check if cc65's `<c64.h>` already provides a named
struct field for it — it usually does.

